# Local development environment for `go run ./test`.
#
# Copy this file to test/.env and fill in what you need. test/.env is
# gitignored; this template is not, so never put a real secret in here.
#
#     cp test/.env.example test/.env
#
# Every name is the same setting as the matching flag, upper-cased with the
# SCHMERZ_ prefix: --push-private-key is SCHMERZ_PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY. Anything
# exported in your shell wins over this file.
#
# Nothing here is needed for an ordinary local run: the launcher starts the
# services with --development, which switches console authentication off.

# --- Console: which roles the local editor holds -------------------------
# With authentication off, everybody is one stand-in identity. By default it
# is in the administrators' group and sees everything. Name other groups here
# to see the console as somebody with fewer roles does. Each collective and
# organisation has two groups, named from its address when it was created:
#   schmerz-collective-<slug>-admins      edits the collective, picks authors
#   schmerz-collective-<slug>-authors     writes topics, updates and actions
#   schmerz-organisation-<slug>-admins    edits the organisation, picks people
#   schmerz-organisation-<slug>-members   belongs to it
# The fixtures' collectives are duesseldorf, koeln, leipzig and sozialstaat.
# SCHMERZ_DEVELOPMENT_GROUPS=schmerz-users,schmerz-collective-duesseldorf-authors

# --- Web Push -------------------------------------------------------------
# A VAPID key pair. Without it notifications are written to each reader's
# list and simply not pushed, which is a supported way to run.
# SCHMERZ_PUSH_PUBLIC_KEY=
# SCHMERZ_PUSH_PRIVATE_KEY=
# SCHMERZ_PUSH_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.org

# --- Who the backend says it is ----------------------------------------
# Every request to a third party (Nominatim, Geoapify, Authentik, push
# services) carries this in its User-Agent, so whoever runs those services
# can write before blocking. It defaults to the Düsseldorf office; a local
# run that hammers a public service should name you instead.
# SCHMERZ_OPERATOR_CONTACT=you@example.org

# --- Reverse geocoding ---------------------------------------------------

# Set to false to make no request to a geocoder at all. Places an editor names
# are never looked up either way; this only affects pins left unnamed.
# SCHMERZ_GEOCODE_ENABLED=true

# --- Sign-in through Authentik (go run ./test -sso) ----------------------
# Where your Authentik is. The console's setup wizard offers it as the
# instance to provision; an issuer URL (…/application/o/<slug>/) is fine too.
# SCHMERZ_OIDC_ISSUER=https://auth.example.org
